<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Anatolia and the Levant</p><h1 class="st-title">Pervaneids</h1><p class="st-meta">1277 CE – 1322 CE · capital Sinop</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Sinop beylik of the family of Mu'in al-Din Suleyman Pervane, the vizier who ruled Seljuk Anatolia under the Mongols.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muin-al-din-suleyman-pervane">Mu'in al-Din Suleyman</a>, known by his title Pervane, was the most powerful man in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/sultanate-of-rum">Sultanate of Rum</a> in the 1260s and 1270s and conquered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> port of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sinope">Sinop</a> in the early 1260s. After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> executed him in 1277 for suspected collusion with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a>, his descendants kept Sinop as a hereditary domain.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muin-al-din-suleyman-pervane">Pervane</a> had built a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/madrasa">madrasa</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sinope">Sinop</a>. His son and grandsons ruled the port and its hinterland as Ilkhanid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a>. The last of them, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi-chelebi">Ghazi Chelebi</a>, was famed for naval raids against the Genoese of <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/genoese-gazaria">Caffa</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/empire-of-trebizond">Empire of Trebizond</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ghazi-chelebi">Ghazi Chelebi's</a> death around 1322, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/sinope">Sinop</a> passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/candarids">Candarids</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/pervaneids.jpg" alt="Pervaneids" width="320" height="173"><figcaption>Image: self- based on WP locator maps · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Candaro%C4%9Fullar%C4%B1.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1277 CE – 1322 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sinop</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mu'in al-Din Suleyman Pervane, Ghazi Chelebi</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Persian, Turkish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Pervaneoğulları, Beylik of Sinop</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1300&amp;focus=pervaneids" aria-label="Pervaneids on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5534 682 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Pervaneids lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5854 938L6134 1224M5854 938L5824 958"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6134 1224h0M5824 958h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5854 938h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5854 938h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Sinop. <a href="/atlas?year=1300&amp;focus=pervaneids">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

